  "cargo-insurance-guide-india": {
    title: "Cargo Insurance in India: Practical Guide for Shippers",
    category: "Compliance",
    date: "August 12, 2026",
    lastUpdated: "August 22, 2026",
    readTime: "6 min read",
    author: "Sanjaya Sahu",
    coverImage: "/blog/og/cargo-insurance-india.svg",
    summary: "Cargo damage, theft, and accidents cost Indian shippers 2-5% of cargo value annually. Learn the difference between carrier liability and cargo insurance, coverage types, claim processes, and how digital freight platforms handle insurance.",
    content: [],
    relatedRoutes: ["rourkela-to-kolkata", "ranchi-to-jamshedpur"],
    faq: [
      { question: "Is cargo insurance mandatory in India?", answer: "Cargo insurance is not legally mandatory under the Motor Vehicles Act, but most commercial shipping contracts and bank letters of credit require it. Carrier liability covers only 5-10 rupees per kg, making additional cargo insurance essential for valuable shipments." },
      { question: "How much does cargo insurance cost in India?", answer: "Premiums range from 0.3% to 2% of declared cargo value. For a 10 lakh rupee shipment, annual premiums are 3,000-20,000 rupees. High-risk cargo (electronics, pharmaceuticals) and long-distance routes command higher premiums." },
      { question: "What does carrier liability cover?", answer: "Under the Motor Vehicles Act, carrier liability covers cargo loss or damage due to the trucker negligence. However, liability is limited to 5-10 rupees per kg of cargo weight, which is far below actual cargo value for most goods." },
      { question: "How do I file a cargo damage claim?", answer: "Document damage immediately with photographs and a joint survey report at delivery. File the claim within 7-30 days with the insurer, submitting transport documents, invoice, packing list, and damage assessment. Settlement typically takes 30-60 days." },
    ],
  },

  "gst-verified-transporters": {
    title: "GST-Verified Transporters: Why It Matters When You Book a Truck Online",
    category: "Compliance",
    date: "September 15, 2026",
    lastUpdated: "September 25, 2026",
    readTime: "7 min read",
    author: "LoadSaathi Team",
    authorBio: "LoadSaathi compliance desk publishes practical guides on GST, e-Way Bills, and freight documentation for Indian shippers and truckers.",
    coverImage: "/blog/og/gst-for-transporters-complete-guide.svg",
    summary: "GST-verified transporters give shippers valid tax invoices, input tax credit, and clean e-Way Bills. As of September 2026, here is how to verify any transporter's GSTIN free on the GST portal before you book.",
    content: [],
    relatedRoutes: ["ranchi-to-kolkata", "bhubaneswar-to-kolkata"],
    keywords: ["gst verified transporters", "check transporter gst number", "gst transport invoice india", "input tax credit freight", "eway bill transporter gstin", "book truck with gst invoice", "gst for transporters", "msme freight gst compliance"],
    faq: [
      { question: "What does GST-verified mean for a transporter?", answer: "It means the transporter's GST registration is shown as Active on the official GST portal. Their invoices carry a valid GSTIN, which lets business shippers claim input tax credit and keeps e-Way Bill details consistent. Verification is free on gst.gov.in under Services, Search Taxpayer, Search by GSTIN." },
      { question: "How do I check a transporter's GST number for free?", answer: "Go to gst.gov.in, open Services, then Search Taxpayer, then Search by GSTIN. Enter the GSTIN from the transporter's quote or invoice. Confirm the trade name matches the business you are dealing with and that the status is Active. No login or fee is required, and the check takes about a minute as of September 2026." },
      { question: "Can I claim input tax credit on freight charges?", answer: "Yes, when a GST-registered transporter issues a compliant invoice and the normal ITC conditions are met. Whether GST on freight is charged by the transporter under forward charge or paid by you under reverse charge depends on the status of both parties, so confirm the treatment with your accountant alongside the invoice." },
      { question: "GST kitna lagta hai truck transport pe?", answer: "September 2026 tak ke rules ke mutabik, ek registered goods transport agency freight par 5% (bina input tax credit) ya 12% (input tax credit ke saath) option charge kar sakta hai, aur ye option invoice par likha hona chahiye. Registration threshold aam states me 40 lakh rupees hai. Exact liability forward charge ya reverse charge me decide hoti hai, isliye invoice par GSTIN aur rate dono verify karein." },
      { question: "Kya bina GST bill ke truck book karna chahiye?", answer: "Avoid karein. 50,000 rupees se upar consignment value ke liye e-Way Bill mandatory hai, jisme transporter GSTIN ya enrollment ID lagti hai. Bina GST invoice ke aap input tax credit nahi le paate, dispute me documented proof nahi bachta, aur checkpoint par document mismatch ka risk rehta hai. GST-verified transporter se booking confirm karein." },
    ],
  },

  "what-is-load-board": {
    title: "What Is a Truck Load Board? Find Loads & Return Trips in India",
    category: "Trucker Tips",
    date: "September 12, 2026",
    lastUpdated: "September 25, 2026",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    author: "LoadSaathi Team",
    authorBio: "LoadSaathi team explains how digital freight matching works for Indian truckers and MSME shippers, corridor by corridor.",
    coverImage: "/blog/og/digital-load-boards-india.svg",
    summary: "Learn how truck load boards connect truck drivers with available goods. Understand return loads, freight matching and how transporters can find their next trip.",
    content: [],
    relatedRoutes: ["ranchi-to-kolkata", "rourkela-to-kolkata"],
    keywords: ["load board india", "what is a load board", "truck load matching platform", "freight matching india", "return loads india", "book truck online india", "empty miles trucking india", "part load matching"],
    faq: [
      { question: "Load board kya hota hai?", answer: "Load board ek online marketplace hai jahan shipper apna load post karta hai aur trucker apni khaali truck ki details post karta hai. Route, weight, vehicle type aur date dekh kar dono side baat karte hain aur deal fix karte hain. Ye transport-nagar ki physical wall ka digital version hai, jaise September 2026 me app-based platforms kaam karte hain." },
      { question: "Load board aur transport broker me kya farak hai?", answer: "Broker shipment ki poori zimmedari leta hai aur margin par sab arrange karta hai. Load board aapko visibility aur tools deta hai, carrier aur terms aap khud choose karte hain. Brokers complex lanes ke liye comfortable hain, direct matching routine corridor runs ke liye zyada control aur rate transparency deti hai." },
      { question: "How does a load board match a truck to a shipment?", answer: "Both sides are geocoded, a road route is calculated, and postings are filtered by capacity, vehicle type, and departure window. Surviving pairs are scored on route overlap, capacity fit, price alignment, timing, and carrier track record. The strongest pairs are surfaced first, and once a request is accepted, chat, payment, and tracking open for that booking." },
      { question: "Are load boards free to use in India?", answer: "Models vary. Some charge truckers a monthly subscription, some take a commission per completed load, some are free for carriers and monetise shipper-side features, and broker-private boards charge per posting. Before paying, confirm the board covers your corridors, verifies its postings, and protects payment until delivery." },
      { question: "How do load boards reduce empty kilometres?", answer: "They make the return leg visible before the truck commits to the outbound trip. India's Ministry of Road Transport and Highways estimates over 35% of commercial truck-kilometres run empty, so posting the return load on a board turns a blind leg into a booked one. Pair boards with route planning tactics from our return loads guide for the full picture." },
    ],
  },
